<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\StackContract.Engine\StackContract.Engine.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\StackContract.Core\StackContract.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="README.md" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" Version="2.0.0-beta4.22272.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>stackcontract</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>stackcontract</PackageId>
    <RootNamespace>StackContract.Cli</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>StackContract.Cli</AssemblyName>
    <Version>0.1.2</Version>
    <Authors>Manuwel Munyai</Authors>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/munyaimanuwel/stackcontract</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/munyaimanuwel/stackcontract</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>dotnet;docker-compose;cli;config;aspnetcore;env;ci;appsettings</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <Description>Local-first .NET global tool that checks a stack/config contract before runtime.

stackcontract validates Docker Compose and/or appsettings against a stackcontract.yml contract, then reports missing services, env keys, and configuration paths. It does not start containers and does not need a Docker daemon for `validate`. Local .env and appsettings are inspected for key/path presence only — values never appear in text or JSON output. Compose is optional for plain C# / ASP.NET apps.

Commands: `stackcontract init` writes a contract from compose and/or appsettings (and optional Options assemblies); `stackcontract validate [--strict] [--environment NAME]` checks the live tree; `stackcontract version` prints the tool version. Exit codes: 0 ok/warnings, 1 any error, 2 usage/parse. Finding codes include SVC_MISSING, ENV_*, CONFIG_PATH_MISSING, CONFIG_PARSE, COMPOSE_PARSE, CONTRACT_INVALID, PROFILE_UNKNOWN.

Legacy ComposeContract names still work: composecontract.yml is accepted when stackcontract.yml is absent. MIT licensed. Not affiliated with Docker, Inc.

Install: `dotnet tool install -g stackcontract`. Pair with StackContract.AspNetCore to fail host start when required configuration keys are missing.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.1.2: Appsettings engine — validate required JSON configuration paths from appsettings.json + appsettings.{Environment}.json. Compose is optional for non-Docker .NET apps. New finding codes CONFIG_PATH_MISSING, CONFIG_PATH_OPTIONAL_MISSING, CONFIG_PARSE. CLI --appsettings / --environment. Sample: samples/aspnet-appsettings.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
